gosh seam 15: The core's state synchronisation is a domain, StateSync: its ABI at the top of src/statesync, its inside under imp/.

For:   REQ21/SHAPE-1, the core factored into domains by the seam, state synchronisation after the
       transport. The lint holds it (seam/DOMAINS): the rest of the core uses it only by
       completeterminal.h and user.h. Until now it declared into two other domains' namespaces,
       the terminal's (Complete) and the transport's (UserStream), so neither boundary could be
       told from a name.
What:  Moves, and renames of where names are, and nothing else: no byte of the protocol, and no
       behaviour, changes. completeterminal.cc and user.cc are moved under src/statesync/imp/ by
       git's renames. Terminal::Complete is StateSync::Complete, and Network::UserStream,
       UserEvent and UserEventType are StateSync's; Complete names the terminal's Framebuffer as
       Terminal::Framebuffer, where it had been in Terminal. Their users say StateSync::
       (mosh-server.cc, stmclient.*, and the core's examples and terminal fuzzer).
Where: src/statesync/ (Makefile.am, completeterminal.h, user.h; imp/); src/frontend/mosh-server.cc,
       stmclient.cc, stmclient.h; src/examples/benchmark.cc, ntester.cc, termemu.cc;
       src/fuzz/terminal_fuzzer.cc.
Kind:  two files moved; two headers' namespace changed; their users qualified.
From:  the core at the pin: src/statesync/{completeterminal.cc,user.cc}.
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.

